   }
  },
  {
   "index": 28,
   "tag": "p",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 163,
   "text": "The default behavior of a kubelet is to fail to start if swap memory is detected on a node.\nThis means that swap should either be disabled or tolerated by kubelet.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 2961,
    "height": 48,
    "widthFraction": 0.49,
    "leftFraction": 0.2,
    "pageFraction": 0.39,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 29,
   "tag": "ul",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 639,
   "text": "To tolerate swap, add failSwapOn: false to kubelet configuration or as a command line argument.\nNote: even if failSwapOn: false is provided, workloads wouldn't have swap access by default.\nThis can be changed by setting a swapBehavior, again in the kubelet configuration file. To use swap,\nset a swapBehavior other than the default NoSwap setting.\nSee Swap memory management for more details.\nTo disa",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 2,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 0,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.03,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 3025,
    "height": 196,
    "widthFraction": 0.49,
    "leftFraction": 0.2,
    "pageFraction": 0.4,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 30,
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": "installing-runtime",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 30,
   "text": "Installing a container runtime",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 1,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 0,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 3189,
    "height": 118,
    "widthFraction": 0.49,
    "leftFraction": 0.2,
    "pageFraction": 0.42,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 31,
   "tag": "p×4",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 465,
   "text": "To run containers in Pods, Kubernetes uses a\ncontainer runtime.\nBy default, Kubernetes uses the\nContainer Runtime Interface (CRI)\nto interface with your chosen container runtime.\nIf you don't specify a runtime, kubeadm automatically tries to detect an installed\ncontainer runtime by scanning through a list of known endpoints.\nIf multiple or no container runtimes are detected kubeadm will throw an e",
   "counts": {
    "links": 2,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 4,
    "repeats": 4,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.09,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 3324,
    "height": 218,
    "widthFraction": 0.49,
    "leftFraction": 0.2,
    "pageFraction": 0.44,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 32,
   "tag": "div",
   "class": "alert alert-info",
   "role": "note",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 362,
   "text": "See container runtimes\nfor more information.\nNote:\nDocker Engine does not implement the CRI\nwhich is a requirement for a container runtime to work with Kubernetes.\nFor that reason, an additional service cri-dockerd\nhas to be installed. cri-dockerd is a project based on the legacy built-in\nDocker Engine support that was removed from the kubelet in version 1.24.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 4,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 1,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 1,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
